1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,936
Hamburgers, egg pancakes, sizzling noodles

2
00:00:02,936 --> 00:00:05,873
Rice balls, toast, and savory soy milk

3
00:00:05,873 --> 00:00:09,076
There are so many delicious breakfasts
around the world

4
00:00:09,076 --> 00:00:13,614
I'm going to collect them all in my
breakfast truck

5
00:00:13,614 --> 00:00:14,348
And so,

6
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:16,216
Beelu, who loves breakfast,

7
00:00:16,216 --> 00:00:18,752
set off on an adventure to collect

8
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:20,554
all kinds of breakfast!

9
00:00:55,722 --> 00:00:57,658
That was fun!

10
00:01:00,193 --> 00:01:02,062
Let's find breakfast!

11
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:04,798
Good morning, Beelu! Good morning, kids!

12
00:01:04,798 --> 00:01:07,868
Today's breakfast is a rice ball

13
00:01:07,868 --> 00:01:09,803
In the adventure story coming up,

14
00:01:09,803 --> 00:01:12,472
there will be three rice ball stickers

15
00:01:12,472 --> 00:01:13,874
Help Beelu

16
00:01:13,874 --> 00:01:16,076
find where they are!

17
00:01:16,076 --> 00:01:18,545
Let's collect today's breakfast!

18
00:01:24,217 --> 00:01:26,219
What should we have for breakfast today?

19
00:01:26,219 --> 00:01:28,155
Go! Go!

20
00:01:28,155 --> 00:01:30,824
Go! Go! Go! Go!

21
00:01:30,824 --> 00:01:32,225
Where is he going?

22
00:01:34,227 --> 00:01:36,496
You can't go that way!

23
00:01:36,496 --> 00:01:37,631
Fly over it!

24
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,172
What are you doing?

25
00:01:45,172 --> 00:01:47,374
Can't you see the bridge is broken?

26
00:01:47,374 --> 00:01:49,176
Of course I know that

27
00:01:49,176 --> 00:01:50,510
I just have to go fast enough

28
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:52,312
and I'll fly right over it

29
00:01:52,312 --> 00:01:53,647
I'm a bird, after all!

30
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:59,319
Then why do you have to cross this bridge?

31
00:01:59,319 --> 00:02:01,922
Because I'm running out of time

32
00:02:01,922 --> 00:02:03,857
I have to make rice balls

33
00:02:05,525 --> 00:02:08,328
for Customer Number One across the bridge

34
00:02:10,530 --> 00:02:14,067
All right, this time I'll make it across!

35
00:02:14,067 --> 00:02:16,269
You can't fly across

36
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:19,072
I'll give you a ride

37
00:02:19,072 --> 00:02:21,141
My breakfast truck is really fast

38
00:02:22,075 --> 00:02:23,810
Oh, good idea!

39
00:02:27,214 --> 00:02:28,215
I'm Chengcheng

40
00:02:28,215 --> 00:02:29,883
What's your name?

41
00:02:29,883 --> 00:02:31,485
I'm Beelu

42
00:02:31,485 --> 00:02:32,419
Okay

43
00:02:35,689 --> 00:02:38,625
Beelu, you're Customer Number Two

44
00:02:38,625 --> 00:02:41,962
When we get across, I'll treat you to a
rice ball

45
00:02:41,962 --> 00:02:43,563
Really?

46
00:02:43,563 --> 00:02:46,233
Mm-hmm. I keep my promises

47
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,169
Oh, it's so sticky!

48
00:02:49,169 --> 00:02:49,970
Let's go, let's go!

49
00:02:49,970 --> 00:02:51,838
Or we'll be late

50
00:02:51,838 --> 00:02:53,640
Is this the button to move forward?

51
00:02:53,640 --> 00:02:54,374
That's right

52
00:02:54,374 --> 00:02:56,109
Then we can definitely make it this time

53
00:02:56,109 --> 00:02:56,843
Huh?

54
00:03:02,449 --> 00:03:04,651
Didn't you say the breakfast truck was
fast?

55
00:03:04,651 --> 00:03:05,852
What I meant was...

56
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:08,121
We can take another route

57
00:03:25,072 --> 00:03:28,275
Darn! If we don't get up there soon,

58
00:03:28,275 --> 00:03:29,876
we'll be too late

59
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:36,016
Chengcheng, you can't fly up there

60
00:03:36,016 --> 00:03:38,752
Of course I can. I'm a bird!

61
00:03:43,690 --> 00:03:46,359
Let's do the Breakfast Brain Workout

62
00:03:46,359 --> 00:03:48,428
and think of a way to help Chengcheng!

63
00:03:50,163 --> 00:03:53,633
Circle your left hand, circle your right hand

64
00:03:53,633 --> 00:03:55,635
Clap! Clap!

65
00:03:55,635 --> 00:03:56,236
Jump up!

66
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:57,504
Jump up!

67
00:03:57,504 --> 00:04:01,041
Move your left brain, move your right
brain

68
00:04:01,041 --> 00:04:03,577
Clap! Clap!

69
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:06,046
Bi Ru Akokay

70
00:04:08,448 --> 00:04:10,317
Look carefully all around you

71
00:04:14,588 --> 00:04:17,257
Chengcheng, there's a path up the mountain
here

72
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,393
Oh, great!

73
00:04:24,331 --> 00:04:26,266
Ready? Let's go!

74
00:04:27,534 --> 00:04:30,270
This is so painful!

75
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:33,473
Please, you have to help us!

76
00:04:33,473 --> 00:04:35,008
I'm in so much pain!

77
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:39,012
A ghost!

78
00:04:39,012 --> 00:04:39,746
Hurry, hurry!

79
00:04:39,746 --> 00:04:42,949
Wait! Help me!

80
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:44,684
Save us!

81
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:46,553
Help us!

82
00:04:48,488 --> 00:04:50,023
Turn around! Turn around!

83
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:52,092
Don't go!

84
00:04:52,092 --> 00:04:53,760
Help us!

85
00:04:54,761 --> 00:04:57,364
Help me! Help me!

86
00:04:59,499 --> 00:05:02,569
Wait! Help me!

87
00:05:02,569 --> 00:05:04,971
Don't come near! Don't come near!

88
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:09,176
Help me!

89
00:05:09,176 --> 00:05:12,312
Please take the plastic bags off us

90
00:05:13,113 --> 00:05:16,316
Huh? Plastic bags?

91
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,118
Beelu, don't go!

92
00:05:18,118 --> 00:05:19,786
Beelu! Beelu!

93
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,789
Don't leave me all alone!

94
00:05:24,524 --> 00:05:27,460
Beelu, I'll treat you to a rice ball!

95
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:28,728
Plastic bags?

96
00:05:29,796 --> 00:05:31,598
Great! Thank you!

97
00:05:32,465 --> 00:05:35,335
Huh? So all of you are...

98
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:36,736
There's so much trash here

99
00:05:36,736 --> 00:05:38,939
that we can't get the plastic bags off
ourselves

100
00:05:38,939 --> 00:05:42,209
Please help us!

101
00:05:42,209 --> 00:05:44,544
I really want to help

102
00:05:44,544 --> 00:05:47,147
But I'm going to be late

103
00:05:47,147 --> 00:05:50,016
Please!

104
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:52,152
But there are so many of you

105
00:05:52,152 --> 00:05:55,021
Taking them off one by one would take too
long

106
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:56,489
We won't make it in time

107
00:05:56,489 --> 00:05:59,025
What should I do?

108
00:06:00,694 --> 00:06:04,097
Chengcheng, let's do the Breakfast Brain
Workout

109
00:06:04,097 --> 00:06:06,900
and think of a way to get there on time!

110
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:09,035
The Breakfast Brain Workout?

111
00:06:09,035 --> 00:06:10,971
That's right. This time,

112
00:06:10,971 --> 00:06:12,973
everyone has to dance together

113
00:06:30,657 --> 00:06:32,392
It's Brain Workout Time!

114
00:06:32,392 --> 00:06:36,062
Circle your left hand, circle your right hand

115
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,731
Clap! Clap!

116
00:06:37,797 --> 00:06:38,331
Jump up!

117
00:06:38,331 --> 00:06:39,132
Jump up!

118
00:06:39,132 --> 00:06:39,399
Jump up!

119
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:39,666
Jump up!

120
00:06:39,799 --> 00:06:43,536
Move your left brain, move your right
brain

121
00:06:43,536 --> 00:06:45,472
Clap! Clap!

122
00:06:45,538 --> 00:06:45,739
Jump up!

123
00:06:45,739 --> 00:06:45,939
Jump up!

124
00:06:45,939 --> 00:06:47,140
Jump up!

125
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:50,810
Make a sun with your hands and say good
morning

126
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:52,812
Clap! Clap!

127
00:06:52,812 --> 00:06:55,415
Bi Ru Akokay

128
00:06:57,884 --> 00:07:00,687
Chengcheng, I've got a good idea!

129
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:19,706
The sticky rice balls are ready

130
00:07:19,706 --> 00:07:21,308
Next...

131
00:07:32,519 --> 00:07:33,987
All cleaned up!

132
00:07:35,188 --> 00:07:37,390
Thank you so much!

133
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,658
You're welcome!

134
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:40,727
Beelu, let's hurry and go!

135
00:07:40,727 --> 00:07:41,461
Okay!

136
00:07:43,863 --> 00:07:45,665
S-sorry!

137
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,804
What should we do? We're really going to
be late!

138
00:07:52,205 --> 00:07:54,541
This time, let us help you!

139
00:08:09,689 --> 00:08:11,291
Done!

140
00:08:14,227 --> 00:08:15,362
The wind is coming!

141
00:08:19,032 --> 00:08:20,700
Thank you!

142
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:21,968
Bye-bye!

143
00:08:44,991 --> 00:08:47,727
Number One, your rice balls are ready!

144
00:08:47,727 --> 00:08:49,396
Thank you, Miss!

145
00:08:49,396 --> 00:08:52,265
Didn't you say the bridge was broken? How
did you get here?

146
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:55,135
Because I keep my promises

147
00:08:56,069 --> 00:08:57,470
Thank you, Chengcheng

148
00:08:58,405 --> 00:09:01,608
Oh, it's nothing

149
00:09:01,608 --> 00:09:02,409
Here

150
00:09:02,609 --> 00:09:04,677
Beelu, your rice ball is ready

151
00:09:04,677 --> 00:09:06,212
Thank you!

152
00:09:06,212 --> 00:09:08,281
Time to eat!

153
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,484
It's so delicious!

154
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:16,623
That was fun!

155
00:09:23,029 --> 00:09:24,898
Let's find breakfast!

156
00:09:24,898 --> 00:09:26,699
Here are the answers!

157
00:09:26,699 --> 00:09:29,436
Today's breakfast stickers are in these
places

158
00:09:33,373 --> 00:09:34,707
Did you find them?

159
00:09:37,644 --> 00:09:40,113
Yeah, I knew it!

160
00:09:41,781 --> 00:09:44,517
How do you make a delicious rice ball?

161
00:09:44,517 --> 00:09:45,185
First,

162
00:09:45,185 --> 00:09:47,253
you need a bucket of tasty glutinous rice

163
00:09:49,189 --> 00:09:49,989
Scoop some out

164
00:09:51,257 --> 00:09:52,192
Spread it flat

165
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:56,463
Add pickled mustard greens and dried
radish

166
00:09:57,664 --> 00:09:58,865
Sprinkle on some pork floss

167
00:10:01,868 --> 00:10:05,405
Add a braised egg and a Chinese cruller

168
00:10:08,475 --> 00:10:10,610
Finally, use just the right amount of
pressure

169
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:13,279
Press and squeeze, squeeze and press

170
00:10:13,813 --> 00:10:16,082
And a delicious rice ball is ready!

171
00:10:16,082 --> 00:10:17,951
Be careful, it's hot when you eat it!

172
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:20,820
Wow, it looks delicious!

173
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:27,026
Huh?

174
00:10:27,894 --> 00:10:29,496
The rice is so sticky!

175
00:10:29,496 --> 00:10:32,432
It sticks to everything if you're not
careful

176
00:10:32,432 --> 00:10:34,968
That's right. Rice is very sticky

177
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:37,103
It can stick lots of things together

178
00:10:37,103 --> 00:10:38,705
For example, in the past,

179
00:10:38,705 --> 00:10:41,508
people flattened rice to seal envelopes

180
00:10:43,243 --> 00:10:46,112
And if you mix glutinous rice,

181
00:10:46,112 --> 00:10:49,249
sand, water, and lime together,

182
00:10:49,249 --> 00:10:52,051
you can make the material people used to
build houses:

183
00:10:52,051 --> 00:10:53,586
sticky-rice mortar

184
00:10:53,586 --> 00:10:56,990
It's a super-strong glue!

185
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:59,659
Oh, super-strong glue?

186
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:00,660
That's right

187
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:04,197
This super-strong glue made from rice

188
00:11:04,197 --> 00:11:07,800
made houses resistant to pressure and very
sturdy

189
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:08,735
When the old city gates in Hengchun,
Taiwan,

190
00:11:08,735 --> 00:11:11,404
were first built,

191
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:14,407
they used this kind of super-strong glue

192
00:11:14,407 --> 00:11:16,609
Part of the Great Wall of China

193
00:11:16,609 --> 00:11:17,810
was also built

194
00:11:17,810 --> 00:11:20,947
using this kind of super-strong glue

195
00:11:21,881 --> 00:11:23,149
That's so cool!

196
00:11:23,149 --> 00:11:26,085
But if you use rice as glue,

197
00:11:26,085 --> 00:11:27,820
aren't you wasting food?

198
00:11:29,289 --> 00:11:32,158
As long as the rice is put to good use,

199
00:11:32,158 --> 00:11:34,093
whether it's made into food to eat

200
00:11:34,093 --> 00:11:36,162
or used to build houses,

201
00:11:36,162 --> 00:11:37,764
it isn't really being wasted

202
00:11:37,764 --> 00:11:41,034
Oh, that's true

203
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:42,769
But I still think rice

204
00:11:42,769 --> 00:11:45,305
is best used to make rice balls

205
00:11:45,305 --> 00:11:48,107
Chengcheng, can I have another one?

206
00:11:48,107 --> 00:11:49,709
Of course!
